  "description_html": "Illustration of a juvenile <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus_rex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus rex\">Tyrannosaurus rex</a></i>.\n<p>Most of this restoration is mostly inspired from the models of 1-year old <i>Tyrannosaurus</i> from the exhibition \"<i>T.rex</i>: The Ultimate Predator\" at American Museum of Natural History, New York (2019-2021).<sup id=\"cite_ref-AMNH_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AMNH-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<sup id=\"cite_ref-AMNH_2_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AMNH_2-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and the juvenile <i>Tarbosaurus</i> MPC-D 107/7 (2-3 years old at death).<sup id=\"cite_ref-Tsuihiji_et.al_2011_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Tsuihiji_et.al_2011-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"References\">References</h2></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-AMNH-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-AMNH_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.amnh.org/exhibitions/t-rex-the-ultimate-predator\">[1]</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-AMNH_2-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-AMNH_2_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2019/03/07/arts/design/t-rex-exhibition-american-museum-of-natural-history.html\">[2]</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Tsuihiji_et.al_2011-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Tsuihiji_et.al_2011_3-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Tsuihiji T <i>et.al</i> (2011). \"Cranial osteology of a juvenile specimen of Tarbosaurus bataar (